<header><h1>The Clan of Saar: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_saar">The Clan of Saar</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="scavenge"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Scavenge">Scavenge</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Saar player gains control of multiple planets during one invasion, the trade goods are gained one at a time.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Mentak Coalition use the &lsquo;Pillage&rsquo; faction ability for each time the Saar gain a trade good from the &lsquo;Scavenge&rsquo; faction ability in a single turn &hellip;? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the Saar player gains control of a planet that is not already controlled by another player, they will explore it before gaining the trade good from this ability.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 25.1c: &ldquo;When a player gains control of a planet that is not already controlled by another player, they explore&rdquo; it.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the Saar player is to gain control of multiple planets not already controlled by another player, they will gain and explore one planet and gain a trade good before gaining and exploring the next.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 35.2d: &ldquo;If a player gains control of multiple planets &hellip; they choose the order in which they resolve those explorations, completely resolving each exploration card before resolving the next.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the Saar player has the <a href="/F_naaz_rokha">Naaz&ndash;Rokha</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, and they gain control of a planet that was controlled by another player, they may explore it or gain a trade good in either order.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Saar player does not gain trade goods from <sc>Scavenge</sc> for the planets in their home system at the start of the game, as they begin the game in control of those planets rather than gaining control of them.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do I control both planets in my home system at the start &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Because you begin with control rather than gaining it, abilities like Saar&rsquo;s Scavenge don&rsquo;t trigger at setup.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="nomadic"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Nomadic">Nomadic</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="raghs-call"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Ragh%27s%20Call">Ragh&rsquo;s Call</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Playing <i>Ragh&rsquo;s Call</i> will prevent ground combat from occurring on that planet.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any PDS on the planet remain. They might produce hits during the <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> step.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>All of the Saar player&rsquo;s ground forces must be placed on the same planet.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Saar&rsquo;s Ragh&rsquo;s Call work in an invasion?&rdquo;: &ldquo;moves the Saar ground forces from one planet to another single planet&rdquo; Ragh&rsquo;s Call moves all Saar ground forces to a single planet.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="chaos-mapping"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Chaos%20Mapping">Chaos Mapping</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A unit may be produced on each of the Saar player&rsquo;s turns.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Saar&rsquo;s Chaos Mapping production work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;At the start of each of your turns, including the turn you pass, you may produce one unit.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;&rsquo;Chaos Mapping&rsquo; can be used as many times as you have turns during the action phase.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>A unit may be produced on the turn the Saar player passes.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Clan of Saar&rsquo;s &lsquo;Chaos Mapping&rsquo; faction-specific technology be used on the turn that the Saar player passes? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;including the turn you pass.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The produced unit must be paid for.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;a unit that is produced must always be paid for.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Saar&rsquo;s Chaos Mapping production work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;you still pay for it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The produced unit may move later that same turn, if the Saar player performs a tactical action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>No unit is using its <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability. The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Sarween_Tools"><i>Sarween Tools</i></a> technology and similar effects will not apply.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Saar&rsquo;s Chaos Mapping production work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;no unit&rsquo;s Production ability is used, so Sarween Tools doesn&rsquo;t apply.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When producing a unit with an ability other than &lsquo;Production,&rsquo; does the price reduction from the &lsquo;Sarween Tools&rsquo; technology apply? A: No, &lsquo;Sarween Tools&rsquo; is only used with the &lsquo;Production&rsquo; ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may still use abilities such as action cards or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/PDS#Upgraded_Unit:~:text=Deep%20Space%20Cannon"><sc>Deep Space Cannon</sc></a> that affect the Saar player&rsquo;s units located in asteroid fields.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an asteroid field contains only non&ndash;ship units belonging to the Saar player, it may still be activated by other players.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player may place a wormhole token in an asteroid field that contains the Saar player&rsquo;s ships, but still cannot activate that system while <i>Chaos Mapping</i> applies.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Creuss use a wormhole token to get into an asteroid field protected by Saar&rsquo;s Chaos Mapping?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Creuss can place the token there but still can&rsquo;t activate the system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="floating-factory"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A Floating Factory does not count toward the Saar player&rsquo;s fleet pool.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Are Saar Floating Factories ships, and do they count against the fleet pool?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; Floating Factories are never ships &hellip; They don&rsquo;t count against your fleet pool.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>There is no limit to the number of Floating Factories that may be in the same system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Saar Floating Factories move and produce in the same action, and how many can share a system?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Any number can share a system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When a Floating Factory produces ground forces, they may be placed in the space area or on a planet they control in that system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Where are produced ground forces placed?&rdquo;: &ldquo;If the producing unit is in space, like a Saar Floating Factory &hellip;, they can go in that space area or on any planet you control in the system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A Floating Factory may move into the active system and use its <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability during the same tactical action.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Saar Floating Factories move and produce in the same action, and how many can share a system?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; nothing requires a dock to start the turn in the active system, so a Floating Factory can move in, carry ground forces to invade, and produce.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When resolving an ability of the <a href="/R_construction"><i>Construction</i></a> strategy card, the Saar player must control a planet in the system they place a Floating Factory in.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Where do Saar Floating Factories go, and how many can share a system?&rdquo;: &ldquo;If an effect places a space dock on a planet, choose the planet as the effect says, then the Floating Factory&rsquo;s own rule puts it in that system&rsquo;s space area.&rdquo; Saar still needs a planet for Construction; implicit.</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (sigmazero13, Aug 1, 2018): &ldquo;So while it is never placed on the planet, an eligible planet does need to exist.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Saar player cannot place a Floating Factory in a system if the only planet they control in that system has the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Demilitarized%20Zone"><i>Demilitarized Zone</i></a> cultural exploration card attached.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Game effects that affect ship movement, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Gravity_Drive"><i>Gravity Drive</i></a> technology, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Flank%20Speed"><i>Flank Speed</i></a> action card, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Light/Wave_Deflector"><i>Light/Wave Deflector</i></a> technology, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors"><i>Antimass Deflectors</i></a> technology, etc, may affect Floating Factories.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Are Saar Floating Factories ships &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;every ability that affects movement, such as Gravity Drive, Flank Speed, Antimass Deflectors or Light/Wave Deflector, still applies to them.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Jan 2018) on Floating Factory movement.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A Floating Factory moving through or out of a gravity rift must roll for removal. It will receive the +1 to its movement.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do movement effects like Gravity Drive and gravity rifts apply to Saar Floating Factories?&rdquo;: &ldquo;they get Gravity Drive, Flank Speed and rift bonuses, and he later confirmed they roll when leaving a gravity rift.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;You still would roll for the Floating Factory.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an effect allows a Floating Factory to move through a system that contains another player&rsquo;s ships (such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Light/Wave_Deflector"><i>Light/Wave Deflector</i></a> technology), it will not be blockaded in systems it moves through.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Hits produced by space cannon rolls cannot be assigned to a Floating Factory.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Clan of Saar&rsquo;s &lsquo;Floating Factories&rsquo; trigger Space Cannon Offense or be assigned hits produced by PDS units? A: No, &lsquo;Floating Factories&rsquo; cannot be the target of PDS fire.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;hits cannot be assigned to it because it is not a ship.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Jan 2018): &ldquo;no&mdash;PDS cannot fire at a Floating Factory when it moves.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Saar player&rsquo;s last ship in a system is destroyed, any Floating Factories in that system are blockaded and destroyed before the <a href="/F_yin">Yin</a> player&rsquo;s agent, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Yin_Brotherhood#Leaders:~:text=Brother%20Milor">Brother Milor</a>, can be resolved to place fighters.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;if Saar loses their last ship in combat but then gets fighters from the Yin agent, is their Floating Factory blockaded during this time? A: Yes, the floating factory is blockaded and would be destroyed prior to Yin agent being resolved.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a Floating Factory is in a system that contains none of the Saar player&rsquo;s ships, and another player moves ships into that system, the Floating Factory is immediately destroyed.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 79.4a: &ldquo;The Clan of Saar&rsquo;s &lsquo;Floating Factory&rsquo; faction-specific space dock is destroyed when it is blockaded.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What happens to a Saar Floating Factory when enemy ships arrive, and can it retreat?&rdquo;: &ldquo;If it is alone with enemy ships, it is destroyed before anything can be done.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (garfielder, Sep 19 2017): &ldquo;if the Saar Space dock was alone when the ships move in, it is destroyed&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>This will happen before the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> step. The Floating Factory is destroyed, even if all of the other player&rsquo; ships are destroyed during this step.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What happens to a Saar Floating Factory when enemy ships arrive, and can it retreat?&rdquo;: &ldquo;it is destroyed before anything can be done.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Saar Floating Factories move and produce in the same action, and how many can share a system?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A Floating Factory is blockaded, and destroyed, the moment enemy ships arrive without Saar ships.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (garfielder, Sep 19 2017), asked whether &ldquo;lonely Space Dock can still be saved if all enemy ships destroyed by Space Cannon fire&rdquo;: &ldquo;I&rsquo;m afraid not&mdash;if the Saar Space dock was alone when the ships move in, it is destroyed, though the space cannons can certainly attempt to avenge it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If all of the other player&rsquo;s ships are removed due to a gravity rift, they will not arrive in the active system. The Floating Factory will not be destroyed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If another player&rsquo;s ships move through a system that contains a Floating Factory and none of the Saar player&rsquo;s ships, the Floating Factory is not destroyed; it is destroyed only if those ships end their movement in that system.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Saar Floating Factories move and produce in the same action, and how many can share a system?&rdquo;: &ldquo;destroyed, the moment enemy ships arrive.&rdquo; Ships passing through do not arrive.</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Yin4Life, 12/10/2018): &ldquo;No, only if you stop in the system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Saar player has their last ship destroyed during combat by a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card, a Floating Factory in the system will be blockaded and destroyed, even if the Saar player produced enough hits to destroy their opponent&rsquo;s remaining ships during that round of combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Players alternate using the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability of their units, one at a time, starting with the active player, and continuing until both players decline, in a row, to use the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> of one of their units. If both the Saar player and their opponent have a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a>, then the first unit to use <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> will be the first unit that may be destroyed by a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a>. If the Saar player&rsquo;s unit is the last to be destroyed, and leaves no other ships in the system, then a Floating Factory in that system will not be blockaded nor destroyed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If, at the end of the combat, the Saar player has no ships, and their opponent has only fighters, then any Floating Factories in the system will be blockaded, and thus destroyed, before the fighters are removed due to lack of capacity.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player has only ground forces participating in the combat as ships due to the effect of their flagship, the Alastor, those ground forces will blockade and destroy any Floating Factories, even if those ground forces are on planets instead of in the space area.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the Saar player announces a retreat during a space combat, but all their ships are destroyed that round, any Floating Factories in that system are destroyed without retreating.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What happens to a Saar Floating Factory when enemy ships arrive, and can it retreat?&rdquo;: &ldquo;If it is alone with enemy ships, it is destroyed.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (garfielder, Sep 19 2017): &ldquo;As a rule, in any situation where a Floating Factory is alone with enemy ships, it is destroyed before it can retreat.&rdquo; Factory with no surviving Saar ships is alone with enemies.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If neither player has ships in the active system after the final round of combat, the Floating Factory is not destroyed, and does not retreat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the Saar player retreats from a space combat, Floating Factories in the active system may retreat with the Saar player&rsquo;s other ships, even if those ships are only fighters. Floating Factories may also be moved by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Skilled%20Retreat"><i>Skilled Retreat</i></a> action card, provided they are never alone with another player&rsquo;s ships.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What happens to a Saar Floating Factory when enemy ships arrive, and can it retreat?&rdquo;: &ldquo;If other Saar ships, even fighters, are with it, it can retreat or Skilled Retreat with them as long as it is never left alone with enemy ships.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The space dock can attempt to retreat with the other ships (in this case&mdash;just its own fighters).&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A Floating Factory cannot count toward the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Improve%20Infrastructure"><i>Improve Infrastructure</i></a> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_2:~:text=Protect%20the%20Border"><i>Protect the Border</i></a> objectives.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="son-of-ragh"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Flagship:~:text=Son%20of%20Ragh">Son of Ragh</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="captain-mendosa"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Leaders:~:text=Captain%20Mendosa">Captain Mendosa</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The effect of Captain Mendosa occurs when the system is activated.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, interact with abilities that increase movement such as Gravity Drive or Flank Speed? A: Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, will get an errata to &lsquo;WHEN you activate a system.&rsquo; This means other bonuses would be applied after Mendosa takes effect.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Move value modifying effects that trigger after a system is activated, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Flank%20Speed"><i>Flank Speed</i></a> action card or the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Gravity_Drive"><i>Gravity Drive</i></a> technology will not be included in Captain Mendosa&rsquo;s effect.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, interact with abilities that increase movement such as Gravity Drive or Flank Speed? A: Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, will get an errata to &lsquo;WHEN you activate a system.&rsquo; This means other bonuses would be applied after Mendosa takes effect.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Gravity rifts apply the +1 during movement. This modifier will not be included in Captain Mendosa&rsquo;s effect.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, interact with abilities that increase movement such as Gravity Drive or Flank Speed? A: Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, will get an errata to &lsquo;WHEN you activate a system.&rsquo; This means other bonuses would be applied after Mendosa takes effect.&rdquo; A gravity rift&rsquo;s +1 is applied during movement, after Mendosa takes effect.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The nebula effect of setting the move value of all ships in that system to one will be overwritten by Captain Mendosa&rsquo;s effect.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When leaving a Nebula, is Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, applied as a bonus or setting the move value? A: &hellip; Mendosa would be treated as a bonus and would override the Nebula&rsquo;s movement value rule.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="rowl-sarrig"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Leaders:~:text=Rowl%20Sarrig">Rowl Sarrig</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If another player has the Saar player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, this does not allow them to produce fighters at a blockaded space dock, so as to place them elsewhere.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="gurno-aggero"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Leaders:~:text=Gurno%20Aggero">Gurno Aggero</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Leaders:~:text=Armageddon%20Relay">Armageddon Relay</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A unit is not adjacent to the system it is in.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 6.2a: &ldquo;A unit or planet is adjacent to all system tiles that are adjacent to the system tile that contains that unit or planet. a A system is not adjacent to itself.&rdquo; a system is not adjacent to itself, so a unit in it is not adjacent to it.</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do ships in Mecatol Rex&rsquo;s system, or in an anomaly, count as adjacent to it for objectives?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; a system isn&rsquo;t adjacent to itself.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="scavenger-zeta"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Mech:~:text=Scavenger%20Zeta">Scavenger Zeta</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Saar player may perform the <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability or their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Scavenge"><sc>Scavenge</sc></a> ability in either order. If they perform their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Scavenge"><sc>Scavenge</sc></a> ability first, they may pay for the <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability with the gained trade good.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the Saar player gains control of a planet that is not already controlled by another player, they will explore it before the <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability will be able to trigger.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Saar player gains control of multiple planets, they may deploy one Scavenger Zeta to each.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If Saar take several planets in one action, can they deploy a mech on each?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; each planet gained is its own timing window.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="deorbit-barrage"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Breakthrough:~:text=Deorbit%20Barrage">Deorbit Barrage</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Saar player must choose how many resources to spend before rolling any dice.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Saar player chooses which unit the hits get assigned to.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Deorbit Barrage (Breakthrough): Can the Saar player assign two hits to a unit with SUSTAIN DAMAGE? A: Yes, the targeted player uses Sustain Damage when the hit is produced.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the chosen unit has the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, it may be used to cancel the hit.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;the targeted player uses Sustain Damage when the hit is produced.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Saar player may assign multiple hits to the same unit.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;Can the Saar player assign two hits to a unit &hellip;? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>
